{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1544112693,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzODgyODQ3MzA=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3071","origin":"github"},"title":"Option to force run (or containers-run) to save even if {cmd} exits with non-0","message":"I am scripting use of `containers-run`. I know that the command I am to run might fail, and I do want the `run` to fail if it does. But I do want to save outputs (log file from bids-validator) regardless of the output status. ATM I do not see explicit option for that.  I am only instructed in the output to\n```\n[INFO   ] The command had a non-zero exit code. If this is expected, you can save the changes with 'datalad save -r -F .git/COMMIT_EDITMSG .'\n```\nBut that is cumbersome for scripting -- `run` could have exited with non-0 for some other reason (wrong container specified etc), and I would need to parse log to figure out either it was the actual command of interest which has failed.\nSo it would be nice to have some `run` specific option, such as `--always-save` or alike which would save even when command fails.","files":null}]}